Diamond Lab (stella-nova/pages/diamond)
========================================

Credit
  This page is inspired by diamond-webgl by Jeremie Piellard:
  https://github.com/piellardj/diamond-webgl
  That project is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.

What was used
  Only the ideas in the public description of that project: a stone made
  of facet planes, a ray tracer that tests every facet at each bounce,
  Snell's law, Fresnel reflection, total internal reflection, Beer's law,
  dispersion, ASET views and a star-filter sparkle.

What was not used
  No source code, shader code, geometry data or assets of diamond-webgl
  are in this folder. The code here (cuts.js, optics.js, saver.js,
  main.js, shaders/gem.wgsl) is a new program, written for this site in
  2026. It does not derive from the GPL-3.0 code.

Data
  Refractive indices, Abbe numbers and B-G dispersion values are the
  published gemmological reference values (GIA, Gem-A). The colour
  matching fit is from Wyman, Sloan and Shirley, "Simple Analytic
  Approximations to the CIE XYZ Color Matching Functions", JCGT 2013.
  Round brilliant proportions follow Tolkowsky, "Diamond Design", 1919.
